        "# Assignment 1 \u2013 Working with NumPy\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "Practice creating arrays, calculating statistics, and manipulating array shapes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. One-dimensional array\n",
        "Create an array from 1 to 20. Calculate summary statistics and find the indices of values greater than 10."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "arr = np.arange(1, 21)\n",
        "print(\"Array:\", arr)\n",
        "print(\"Sum:\", np.sum(arr))\n",
        "print(\"Mean:\", np.mean(arr))\n",
        "print(\"Median:\", np.median(arr))\n",
        "print(\"Standard deviation:\", np.std(arr))\n",
        "print(\"Indices greater than 10:\", np.where(arr > 10)[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Two-dimensional array\n",
        "Reshape the numbers 1\u201316 into a 4 \u00d7 4 matrix. Transpose it and calculate sums across rows and columns."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "arr2d = np.arange(1, 17).reshape(4, 4)\n",
        "print(\"Original array:\\n\", arr2d)\n",
        "print(\"Transpose:\\n\", arr2d.T)\n",
        "print(\"Row-wise sums:\", arr2d.sum(axis=1))\n",
        "print(\"Column-wise sums:\", arr2d.sum(axis=0))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Random arrays and operations\n",
        "Create two 3 \u00d7 3 arrays with integers from 1 to 20. Compare element-wise operations with the matrix dot product."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "rng = np.random.default_rng(42)  # Fixed seed makes this example reproducible\n",
        "a = rng.integers(1, 21, size=(3, 3))\n",
        "b = rng.integers(1, 21, size=(3, 3))\n",
        "print(\"Array A:\\n\", a)\n",
        "print(\"Array B:\\n\", b)\n",
        "print(\"Addition:\\n\", a + b)\n",
        "print(\"Subtraction:\\n\", a - b)\n",
        "print(\"Element-wise multiplication:\\n\", a * b)\n",
        "print(\"Dot product:\\n\", np.dot(a, b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Reshaping and slicing\n",
        "Reshape 12 values into 3 \u00d7 4, then select the first two rows and last two columns."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "values = np.arange(1, 13)\n",
        "reshaped = values.reshape(3, 4)\n",
        "print(\"Reshaped array:\\n\", reshaped)\n",
        "print(\"First two rows and last two columns:\\n\", reshaped[:2, -2:])"
      ]
    }
